---
import {publicationRows,assertPlacement,displayRow,rightsInUse,sourceFormat,isStale,SECTION_KINDS} from '../../lib/ai-and-jobs.mjs';
const snapshots=Object.values(import.meta.glob('../../../data/ai-and-jobs/*.json',{eager:true,import:'default'})) as any[];
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
// Every published row of a snapshot, read block by block so the placement rule is checked here too.
const rowsFor=(s:any)=>Object.keys(SECTION_KINDS).flatMap(section=>assertPlacement(publicationRows(s,section),section));
const tables=snapshots.map(s=>{const rows=rowsFor(s);return {s,rows,rights:rightsInUse(rows)};});
// The Indeed summary below is printed only while the Indeed rights record is actually in use.
const usesIndeed=tables.some(t=>t.rights.some((r:any)=>r.id==='indeed-ai-tracker'));
---
<section id="ai-and-jobs" class="my-12"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">AI and jobs: figure-level receipts</h2>
{usesIndeed&&<p>Indeed Hiring Lab's AI Tracker, CC BY 4.0. The pinned repository README and licence were read first-hand on 14 November 2026. Daily observations use a seven-day trailing average; source refresh is monthly. Only Indeed postings are covered; these are keyword mentions, not employment effects. No uncertainty published by the source. Every displayed percentage is selected directly from the pinned CSV and rounded for display; the export retains original precision.</p>}
{tables.map(({s,rows,rights})=><><p>Retrieved {s.retrieved_at} · <a href={`${base}ai-and-jobs/archive/${s.retrieved_at}.json`}>Immutable snapshot, method versions, source commit and raw SHA-256</a></p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm"><caption>All published observations: evidence kind, date, method and rights</caption><thead><tr><th>Country / kind</th><th>Period / value</th><th>Vintage / uncertainty</th><th>Source / method / rights</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map((r:any)=>{const d=displayRow(r);const format=sourceFormat(r.source_url);return <tr data-kind={r.kind} data-rights={d.rights_id}><td>{r.series.geography} · {d.kind_caption}</td><td>{r.period} · {d.value_text}</td><td>{r.vintage} · {d.uncertainty_text} · {isStale(r,r.source)?'Stale':'Within refresh window'}</td><td><a href={r.source_url}>{format==='CSV'?'CSV':'Source file'}</a> · <a href={r.version.methodology_url}>Method version</a> · <a href={d.licence_url}>{d.licence}</a></td></tr>;})}</tbody></table></div>
{rights.map((r:any)=><p data-rights-credit={r.id}>Credit: {r.attribution_text} Licence: <a href={r.licence_url}>{r.licence}</a>. Terms read on {r.verified_on}.</p>)}</>)}
<p>Rights remain unconfirmed for unused sources until the specific dataset's terms are read. No ONS, BLS, Anthropic, Eurostat, OECD, ILO or company-claim figures are copied into this section. <a href="https://github.com/koltregaskes/ai-resource-hub/blob/main/docs/AI-AND-JOBS-METHOD.md">Reviewed source policy and data model</a>.</p>
</section>
